---
import MainLayout from "@/components/layout/MainLayout.astro";

const lastUpdated = "27 August 2026";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms for using Small Web Apps: what the free browser-based tools do and do not promise, acceptable use, ownership of your files, advertising, and liability."
  canonicalPath="/terms"
>
  <section class="static-page">
    <div class="static-inner">
      <span class="static-eyebrow">Terms</span>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="static-meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="static-card">
        <p>
          These terms cover your use of <strong>smallwebapps.com</strong> and every tool, guide, and page
          on it (the "site"). The site is operated by <strong>Lucas Diniz</strong> as an independent
          project. Using the site means you accept these terms.
        </p>

        <h2>1. What the site provides</h2>
        <p>
          Small Web Apps is a collection of free utilities that run entirely inside your web browser —
          formatters, converters, generators, calculators, and inspection tools for PDF, image, developer,
          and data workflows — together with written guides explaining how to use them. There are no
          accounts, no sign-up, no paywalls, and no usage limits.
        </p>

        <h2>2. The tools are provided as-is</h2>
        <p>
          The site is offered free of charge and without warranty of any kind, express or implied,
          including any implied warranty of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, or
          non-infringement. Specifically, the site does not promise:
        </p>
        <ul class="static-list">
          <li>uninterrupted or error-free availability;</li>
          <li>that any tool's output is accurate, complete, or suitable for your particular case;</li>
          <li>that a tool will handle files of any given size, format, or complexity;</li>
          <li>that a tool will remain available, unchanged, or backwards-compatible in future.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Several tools are explicitly probabilistic or best-effort — image-origin inspection, for example,
          reports signals and likelihoods, not verdicts. Each tool page documents its own limitations, and
          those limitations form part of these terms.
        </p>

        <h2>3. You are responsible for how you use the output</h2>
        <p>
          You remain responsible for reviewing any output before relying on it, for keeping your own backup
          of any file you process, and for deciding whether a tool is appropriate for your workflow.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Do not use these tools as the sole basis for high-stakes decisions.</strong> Nothing on
          this site is legal, medical, financial, or professional advice. A BMI calculator is not a medical
          assessment, a loan calculator is not a financing offer, and an AI-image check is not proof of a
          file's origin.
        </p>

        <h2>4. Your files stay yours</h2>
        <p>
          Files and text you put into a tool are processed locally in your browser and are never uploaded
          to us. We claim no ownership of, and acquire no licence to, anything you process here — because
          we never receive it. See the <a class="prose-link" href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for detail.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>You agree not to:</p>
        <ul class="static-list">
          <li>use the site for anything unlawful, or to process content you have no right to process;</li>
          <li>attempt to disrupt, overload, probe, or gain unauthorised access to the site or its host;</li>
          <li>scrape, mirror, or automate access in a way that degrades the site for other people;</li>
          <li>remove, obscure, or interfere with advertising, notices, or attribution on the site;</li>
          <li>misrepresent the site or its tools as your own product or as endorsed by anyone.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>6. Advertising</h2>
        <p>
          Advertising is what keeps these tools free. Ads are served by Google AdSense and are placed
          around content, never inside a tool's working area and never disguised as tool controls.
        </p>
        <p>
          You must not click ads to "support" the site, and you must not interact with ads through
          automated, misleading, or incentivized means. Doing so violates Google's policies and harms
          the site.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The Small Web Apps name, design, written guides, and tool copy belong to the site's operator.
          The underlying source code is published on
          <a class="prose-link" href="https://github.com/LucasHenriqueDiniz/smallwebapps" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
          and is governed by the licence stated in that repository. Third-party libraries used by the
          tools remain under their own licences.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Third-party services and links</h2>
        <p>
          The site depends on third-party services — Cloudflare for hosting, Google for advertising — and
          links to external resources such as documentation and Google Takeout. Those services and sites
          operate under their own terms, which the site's operator does not control.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, the site's operator is not liable for any indirect,
          incidental, or consequential damages, or for any loss of data, profit, or business, arising from
          your use of or inability to use the site. Because the site is provided free of charge, total
          liability for any claim relating to it is limited to zero.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some jurisdictions do not allow certain limitations of liability or exclusions of warranty. Where
          that is the case, those limitations apply only to the extent permitted, and your statutory
          consumer rights are unaffected.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Changes and availability</h2>
        <p>
          Tools may be added, changed, or removed at any time, and the site may be taken offline
          temporarily or permanently without notice. These terms may also change; the "last updated" date
          above will reflect that, and continued use after a change means you accept the revised terms.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about these terms can be sent through the
          <a class="prose-link" href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
        </p>

        <div class="static-highlight">
          <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
          <p>
            The short version: free tools, offered honestly and without guarantees. Your files stay on your
            device, you check the output before you rely on it, and you don't click the ads to be nice.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</MainLayout>

<style>
.static-page {
  max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 64px 24px 80px;
  font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif;
}
.static-inner { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px; }
.static-eyebrow {
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
  background: rgba(26,115,232,.1); color: var(--blue);
  padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px;
  font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .1em;
  width: fit-content;
}
h1 {
  font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.6rem); font-weight: 900;
  color: var(--text); letter-spacing: -.5px; line-height: 1.15; margin: 0;
}
.static-meta {
  margin: -8px 0 0; font-size: .82rem; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 500;
}
.static-card {
  background: var(--surface-strong); border: 1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius: 20px; padding: 32px;
  display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px;
  box-shadow: var(--shadow);
}
.static-card p {
  font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--muted); margin: 0;
}
.static-card h2 {
  font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--text);
  margin: 18px 0 0; letter-spacing: -.2px;
}
.static-card h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 8px; }
.static-list {
  margin: 0; padding-left: 20px;
  font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.8; color: var(--muted);
}
.static-list li { margin: 6px 0; }
.static-highlight {
  display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 12px;
  background: rgba(26,115,232,.07); border: 1px solid rgba(26,115,232,.15);
  border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 18px; margin-top: 12px;
  color: var(--blue);
}
.static-highlight svg { flex-shrink: 0; margin-top: 2px; }
.static-highlight p  { color: var(--blue) !important; font-weight: 500; font-size: .88rem !important; line-height: 1.6 !important; }
</style>
